            <ArticleTitle>Sample Power and ExpDesign: tools for improving design of animal experiments.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>39-43</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Proper experimental design, involving the correct number of animals, should be a basic skill for any scientist working with animals. The authors describe a university-developed and freely available tutorial program and an interactive computer-assisted learning program, both of which guide students through the steps necessary for designing animal experiments and estimating optimal sample sizes.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
